   - These capture asymmetry, proportions, and inertia distribution.

4. Higher-Order Metrics: SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS, SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS, KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS, KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS.
   - These provide insights into shape asymmetry and peakedness.

5. Utilization Metrics: PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY, MAX.LENGTH_RECTANGULARITY, HOLLOWS_RATIO.
   - These measure the efficiency of the silhouette in utilizing bounding areas.

Focusing on these groups can guide effective feature engineering and downstream modeling.

